KG42.register("rules-22d66d6b1432a614241673fa",{"id":"30-motivational_game::v141-c-R001","paper":"30-motivational_game","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"A prosumer's surplus serves other peers' demand as the first priority, before sale to the CPS if needed. Scope: Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation of an individual prosumer's surplus. Condition: E_{n,s} > 0. Peer surplus serves a prosumer's energy deficiency first; grid supply is permitted only when no surplus remains in the overall P2P network. Scope: Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation to an energy-deficient prosumer. Condition: E_{n,d} > 0.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation of an individual prosumer's surplus. | Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation to an energy-deficient prosumer.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g03-e001"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer's surplus serves other peers' demand as the first priority, before sale to the CPS if needed. Scope: Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation of an individual prosumer's surplus. Condition: E_{n,s} > 0.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Peer surplus serves a prosumer's energy deficiency first; grid supply is permitted only when no surplus remains in the overall P2P network. Scope: Proposed canonical coalition-game P2P network; allocation to an energy-deficient prosumer. Condition: E_{n,d} > 0.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g03-e001","v141-b-g02-e05"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the prosumer has any surplus, i.e., E_{n,s} > 0, it sells it to meet the demand of other peers as the first priority and then to the CPS, if needed."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 243 (2019) 10–20 Similarly, if there is any electricity deﬁciency, i.e., En , d > 0 ,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required. Thus, in P2P trading, all the prosumers cooperate with one another to trade the surplus energy among themselves as a first priority, and then interact with the grid, if necessary, to sell or buy the total excess or deficient energy respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 How the proposed energy trading scheme can psychologically motivate prosumers","anchor_text":"p the FiT scheme, as considered in this study, a prosumer buys its deﬁcient energy from the grid and","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Under P2P trading, the deﬁcient energy of any prosumer is ﬁrst met by the surplus energy from another peer of the network and a prosumer only consume from the grid if there is no surplus left in the overall peer-to-peer network. Therefore, the demand to the grid is lower in the P2P scheme, which subsequently results in lower CO2 production."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-dd42379cd7-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Development of the trading scheme","anchor_text":"participate. th P2 3.2.2. Development of the trading scheme ps To use a canonical coalition game wit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To use a canonical coalition game with the above properties for designing a P2P trading scheme, it is assumed that a number of prosumers with rooftop solar panels (without batteries) are connected to a central power station (CPS). They are also connected to each other through a secure information system via their smart meters for all necessary communication and transactions of P2P trading. At any particular time, each prosumer n has a particular amount of electricity surplus E_{n,s} from the supply from its solar panel and deficiency E_{n,d}."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No x are declared because the frozen graph for this rule contains only clearing.local and no typed operational/design variable node for peer allocation, CPS residual sale, or grid fallback. The source quantities E_{n,s} and E_{n,d} appear as clearing conditions/state quantities and cannot be attached to an approved variable node without a C.1 graph revision; this does not assert that the source lacks such quantities.","empty_theta_reason":"No theta are declared because the frozen graph supplies no parameter object or parameter node scoped to this rule. Prices and surplus/deficiency quantities are defined elsewhere in the paper or would need explicit C.1-approved parameter representations; this does not assert that the source lacks parameters."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","quote":"If the prosumer has any surplus, i.e., E_{n,s} > 0, it sells it to meet the demand of other peers as the first priority and then to the CPS, if needed."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","quote":"Similarly, if there is any electricity deficiency, i.e., E_{n,d} > 0, a prosumer first buys the necessary amount from the peers within the network and then from the CPS, if required."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e001","quote":"Under P2P trading, the deﬁcient energy of any prosumer is ﬁrst met by the surplus energy from another peer of the network and a prosumer only consume from the grid if there is no surplus left in the overall peer-to-peer network."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"1d162787a7920da62a67a62fc20ca8305a3201934b0d1d397b1d9cec7862e91e","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The supplied evidence supports two conditional clearing priorities: surplus first serves peer demand before CPS sale when E_{n,s}>0, and deficiency is first met by peer surplus with grid purchase only when no surplus remains when E_{n,d}>0. However, the frozen rule graph contains only the unary relation clearing.local with E=[]; it provides no approved variables/parameters or edges for peer allocation, CPS residual sale/purchase, or grid fallback. The source statements are verbal priority rules and do not name allocation quantities that could be used as an expression without inventing mathematics. Existing C.1 constraints are preserved as not_formalized, and precise graph revision is required before a supported expression can be produced.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is the surplus-side priority branch of the frozen clearing.local relation. The only available member vertex is clearing.local; no edge can be attached because the frozen rule graph has E=[] and no allocation or residual-grid nodes."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is the deficiency-side priority branch of the frozen clearing.local relation. The frozen rule graph has no edge or node representing peer-surplus-first allocation followed by grid fallback."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: add an approved typed representation for the clearing-state quantities E_{n,s} (surplus of prosumer n) and E_{n,d} (deficiency of prosumer n), including index n and any source-supported domains/units, or explicitly declare them out of scope for this rule.","C.1: add approved nodes/edges representing the two priority branches owned by clearing.local: peer demand served before CPS sale when E_{n,s}>0, and peer surplus used before grid purchase when E_{n,d}>0, including the residual/fallback relation to the CPS/grid. The frozen E=[] cannot encode either ordering.","C.1/B: provide source-supported symbols and definitions for any allocation quantities (for example peer sale, peer purchase, residual CPS sale/purchase) if an algebraic clearing expression is intended; the supplied text states the priorities verbally and does not name such quantities.","Do not attach this rule to quantities or nodes owned by other rules, such as product.local_energy, bidding.supply, bidding.demand, execution.energy_trade, or pricing.local, unless C.1 explicitly revises v141-c-R001's V/E to include the corresponding source-supported relationships."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
